%description:

Tcp.pmtudEnabled:off -- without DF, the router fragments the segments.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "Path MTU Discovery (RFC 1191, RFC 1981) enabled/disabled".

The classes: on (true, the default) and off (false, the value of LegacyTcp). The code:
TcpConnection::sendToIP() sets DF on each IPv4 segment with true;
TcpConnection::processIcmpv4Error() reduces the MSS at a Fragmentation Needed and sends the
lost segment again. This test separates "off" from "on".

Host under test: host1, which sends 10000 bytes to host2 through the router, whose link to
host2 has an MTU of 1000 bytes; the segments of host1 carry 1500 bytes of IP. Observation: level 1, the first data frame that reaches host2 is the first fragment of a
segment, without DF.

%# parameter: Tcp.pmtudEnabled
%# class: off
%# value: false
%# key: *.host1.tcp.pmtudEnabled
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpPmtudEnabledOff")
        .once(on("host2.eth[0].mac").signal("packetReceivedFromLower")
                  .filterPacket("ipv4.totalLengthField > 100B")
                  .first()
                  .assertPacket("ipv4.dontFragment == false && ipv4.moreFragments == true")
                  .describe("the first data frame at host2")
                  .within(1.0));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpPmtudEnabledOff compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.pmtudEnabled = false    # the parameter under test
network = inet.protocoltest.TapRouterNetwork
*.router.eth[1].mac.mtu = 1000B
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpPmtudEnabledOff: PASS
